 "title": "The filter",
 "text": "A low-pass filter takes the brightness off: what's below CUTOFF passes, what's above is cut. RESONANCE adds a peak at the cutoff. Try: sweep CUTOFF while you play; turn RESONANCE up and sweep again (the classic 'wow'); at the top the filter whistles on its own. Plug KEY into MIDI In's PITCH so high notes stay as bright as low ones.",
